{
    "chapter_num": 7,
    "verses_count": 37,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Tradition of the Elders"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now when the Pharisees gathered together to him, with some of the scribes, who had come from Jerusalem, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "they saw that some of his disciples ate with hands defiled, that is, unwashed. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "(For the Pharisees, and all the Jews, do not eat unless they wash their hands,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "One Greek word is of uncertain meaning and is not translated"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " observing the tradition of the elders; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and when they come from the market place, they do not eat unless they purify"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities read baptize"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " themselves;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities read and they do not eat anything from the market unless they purify it"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and there are many other traditions which they observe, the washing of cups and pots and vessels of bronze."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities add and beds"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": ") "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And the Pharisees and the scribes asked him, “Why do your disciples not live"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Greek walk"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " according to the tradition of the elders, but eat with hands defiled?” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to them, “Well did Isaiah prophesy of you hypocrites, as it is written,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "‘This people honors me with their lips,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "but their heart is far from me;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "in vain do they worship me,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "LINE_BREAK",
                            "text": "\n"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "teaching as doctrines the precepts of men.’"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "You leave the commandment of God, and hold fast the tradition of men.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to them, “You have a fine way of rejecting the commandment of God, in order to keep your tradition! "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For Moses said, ‘Honor your father and your mother’; and, ‘He who speaks evil of father or mother, let him surely die’; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "but you say, ‘If a man tells his father or his mother, What you would have gained from me is Corban’ (that is, given to God)"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or an offering"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "— "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "then you no longer permit him to do anything for his father or mother, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "thus making void the word of God through your tradition which you hand on. And many such things you do.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he called the people to him again, and said to them, “Hear me, all of you, and understand: "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "there is nothing outside a man which by going into him can defile him; but the things which come out of a man are what defile him.”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities add verse 16, “If any man has ears to hear, let him hear”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And when he had entered the house, and left the people, his disciples asked him about the parable. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to them, “Then are you also without understanding? Do you not see that whatever goes into a man from outside cannot defile him, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "since it enters, not his heart but his stomach, and so passes on?”"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or is evacuated"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " (Thus he declared all foods clean.) "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said, “What comes out of a man is what defiles a man. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 21,
                    "num_str": "21",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For from within, out of the heart of man, come evil thoughts, fornication, theft, murder, adultery, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 22,
                    "num_str": "22",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "coveting, wickedness, deceit, licentiousness, envy, slander, pride, foolishness. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 23,
                    "num_str": "23",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "All these evil things come from within, and they defile a man.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "The Syrophoenician Woman’s Faith"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 24,
                    "num_str": "24",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And from there he arose and went away to the region of Tyre and Sidon."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Other ancient authorities omit and Sidon"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " And he entered a house, and would not have any one know it; yet he could not be hid. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 25,
                    "num_str": "25",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But immediately a woman, whose little daughter was possessed by an unclean spirit, heard of him, and came and fell down at his feet. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 26,
                    "num_str": "26",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now the woman was a Greek, a Syrophoeni′cian by birth. And she begged him to cast the demon out of her daughter. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 27,
                    "num_str": "27",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to her, “Let the children first be fed, for it is not right to take the children’s bread and throw it to the dogs.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 28,
                    "num_str": "28",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But she answered him, “Yes, Lord; yet even the dogs under the table eat the children’s crumbs.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 29,
                    "num_str": "29",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he said to her, “For this saying you may go your way; the demon has left your daughter.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 30,
                    "num_str": "30",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And she went home, and found the child lying in bed, and the demon gone."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Jesus Cures a Deaf Man"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 31,
                    "num_str": "31",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then he returned from the region of Tyre, and went through Sidon to the Sea of Galilee, through the region of the Decap′olis. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 32,
                    "num_str": "32",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they brought to him a man who was deaf and had an impediment in his speech; and they besought him to lay his hand upon him. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 33,
                    "num_str": "33",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And taking him aside from the multitude privately, he put his fingers into his ears, and he spat and touched his tongue; "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 34,
                    "num_str": "34",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and looking up to heaven, he sighed, and said to him, “Eph′phatha,” that is, “Be opened.” "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 35,
                    "num_str": "35",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And his ears were opened, his tongue was released, and he spoke plainly. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 36,
                    "num_str": "36",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he charged them to tell no one; but the more he charged them, the more zealously they proclaimed it. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 37,
                    "num_str": "37",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And they were astonished beyond measure, saying, “He has done all things well; he even makes the deaf hear and the dumb speak.”"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}